      "message": "The logic would breaks when pKVM is enabled: the host and pKVM have separate struct dmar_domain instances. intel_iommu_unmap() populates the host\u0027s leaf_cache, while dmar_domain_clear_leaf_cache() only runs inside pKVM, so the host\u0027s leaf_cache is never invalidated when page tables are freed or replaced by superpages.\n\nAlso in upstream 6.19, VT-d map/unmap and pfn_to_dma_pte() have moved to generic_pt, so this legacy page-table code is already going away.",
